export const privacyPolicy = "# KartUP Privacy Policy\n\n_Last updated: 2026-10-20 · TEMPLATE — have it reviewed by a lawyer before publishing._\n\nKartUP (\"we\", \"us\") is operated by KartUP SRL (placeholder company name), Str. Exemplu 1, București, România (placeholder). This policy explains what personal data we process when you use the KartUP mobile app and how you can control it. We act as data controller under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).\n\n## 1. Data we collect\n- **Account data:** email address, password (stored only as a secure hash by our authentication provider), sign-in provider (Apple, Google, Facebook) and the basic profile data that provider shares with us (name, email).\n- **Profile data:** first and last name, date of birth (others see only your age), home city, short bio, profile photo, karting experience per track.\n- **Activity data:** sessions you create or join, lobby chat messages, check-ins, results, points, rank, no-shows and bans, reports you send or receive.\n- **Location:** only at check-in time, and only to confirm that you are within the configured distance of the track. We do not track your location in the background.\n- **Payment data:** payments are processed by Stripe. We receive the amount, status and a payment reference, but never your full card number.\n- **Device data:** push-notification token, app version, language.\n\n## 2. Why we use it (legal basis)\n- To provide the service: accounts, lobbies, payments, refunds, rankings (contract, Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).\n- To keep the community fair and safe: no-show penalties, moderation of reports (legitimate interest, Art. 6(1)(f)).\n- To meet legal obligations: accounting and tax records of payments (Art. 6(1)(c)).\n- To send notifications you can switch off in Settings (consent / legitimate interest).\n\n## 3. Who sees your data\n- **Other users** see your public profile: photo, name, age, city, bio, rank, points, sessions and tracks raced, and an active ban if you have one. Lobby members see lobby chat messages.\n- **Service providers** acting on our instructions: Supabase (hosting, EU region), Stripe (payments), Expo (push delivery), our email provider.\n- **Hosts** of a session receive payouts through Stripe; they do not receive your payment details.\n- We never sell your data.\n\n## 4. How long we keep it\nAccount and profile data: until you delete your account. Payment and refund records: as long as Romanian accounting law requires (currently up to 10 years), without your name after account deletion. Chat messages: until the session is 12 months old.\n\n## 5. Your rights\nYou can access, correct, export or delete your data. You can **delete your account inside the app** (Settings → Delete account). You may object to processing or file a complaint with the Romanian data protection authority (ANSPDCP, www.dataprotection.ro). Contact us at support@kartup.example.\n\n## 6. Minimum age\nYou must be at least 16 years old to use KartUP.\n\n## 7. Changes\nWe will notify you in the app before material changes take effect.\n\n## 8. Contact\nKartUP SRL (placeholder company name) · Str. Exemplu 1, București, România (placeholder) · support@kartup.example\n";
export const termsOfService = "# KartUP Terms of Service\n\n_Last updated: 2026-10-20 · TEMPLATE — have it reviewed by a lawyer before publishing._\n\nThese terms are an agreement between you and KartUP SRL (placeholder company name) (Str. Exemplu 1, București, România (placeholder)) for the use of KartUP. KartUP — Find your team & race.\n\n## 1. The service\nKartUP helps karting enthusiasts find other drivers, join sessions at karting tracks, split the cost, and earn ranking points. We are not a karting track. The track's own safety rules and conditions apply when you drive.\n\n## 2. Accounts\nYou must be at least 16, give accurate information and keep your login safe. One account per person.\n\n## 3. Sessions, hosts and payments\n- A **host** creates a session and is responsible for booking the slot with the track and paying the track.\n- Every participant, including the host, pays their share in the app: the track price per driver plus a **platform fee of 5 RON per driver**. Your seat is held only after a successful payment.\n- After the session has taken place, we pay the host the track price for the seats that were paid and not refunded.\n\n## 4. Cancellations and refunds\n- You can cancel and get a **full automatic refund until 1 hour before the session start**.\n- Within the last hour, cancellation is not possible and no refund is given.\n- If the host, the track or KartUP cancels a session — including automatic cancellation when fewer than 4 drivers have paid — everyone gets a full refund.\n- The host may remove participants who have not paid. A host may remove a paid participant only with a full refund.\n\n## 5. Check-in, no-shows and bans\nParticipants check in at the track (using their location) from 30 minutes before the start until 15 minutes after. Paid participants who neither check in nor are confirmed by the host are marked as **no-show** and temporarily blocked from joining sessions: 1 hour for the first no-show, 24 hours for the second, 7 days for the third and 30 days from the fourth. You can appeal from your profile.\n\n## 6. Results and ranking\nThe host enters the results. Participants have 24 hours to confirm or dispute them; disputed results are reviewed by our team. Points and ranks have no monetary value.\n\n## 7. Community rules — zero tolerance\nNo harassment, hate speech, threats, sexual content, spam or impersonation, in profiles or chat. You can report and block users. We review reports within 24 hours and may remove content and ban accounts.\n\n## 8. Liability\nKarting is a motorsport with inherent risks. KartUP is not responsible for what happens at the track; to the extent permitted by law our liability is limited to the fees you paid us in the last 12 months.\n\n## 9. Ending your account\nYou can delete your account at any time in Settings. We may suspend accounts that break these terms.\n\n## 10. Law\nRomanian law applies. Consumers keep the protections of their country of residence. Contact: support@kartup.example.\n";
